      "section_kind": "chapter_overview",
      "section_title": "Gifts ordered for the gathered church",
      "text": "1 Corinthians 14 compares tongues and prophecy by asking what happens in the gathered assembly. Tongues without interpretation are not understood by others, while prophecy is described as building up, encouraging, and consoling the church. Paul therefore regulates turn-taking, number, interpretation, evaluation, silence, and the participation of the gathered community, closing with the instruction that all things be done decently and in order.",
