      "section_kind": "interpretive_questions",
      "section_title": "Intelligibility, discernment, and silence",
      "text": "The chapter repeatedly treats intelligibility, edification, learning, encouragement, self-control, peace, and communal evaluation as relevant to worship. Tongues are limited and require interpretation; prophets speak in turn and are weighed by others. The commands about women or wives in verses 34–35 are difficult within the chapter's wider pattern and remain disputed, especially because the same letter assumes women pray and prophesy and because some Western witnesses place the verses after verse 40.",
