      "section_kind": "why_it_matters",
      "section_title": "Order serves participation",
      "text": "In this chapter, order is directed toward intelligible participation and peace rather than leader convenience or the suppression of necessary questions. The gathered assembly may contain many contributions, but each is governed by the shared aim of building up the church. That makes interpretation, turn-taking, and discernment part of spiritual practice rather than obstacles to it.",
